1
00:00:15,300 --> 00:00:16,260
Yu-Gi-Oh!

2
00:01:05,180 --> 00:01:09,600
Tell me, Ishizu, do you still
think destiny is on your side?

3
00:01:09,780 --> 00:01:15,060
Or have you finally faced up to the
undeniable truth that this duel is mine?

4
00:01:15,480 --> 00:01:17,656
I have seen the future quite clearly.

5
00:01:18,260 --> 00:01:21,680
Kaiba will lose at the hands
of his own Egyptian god card.

6
00:01:22,520 --> 00:01:24,437
You know, I gotta hand it to her.

7
00:01:24,520 --> 00:01:27,637
She's about to get stunk, but
that Ishizu's keeping her cool.

8
00:01:27,720 --> 00:01:31,277
Yeah, I'm starting to think that maybe
she does know something we don't.

9
00:01:31,360 --> 00:01:32,190
No way.

10
00:01:32,273 --> 00:01:33,357
That's just an act.

11
00:01:33,440 --> 00:01:35,640
Act or no act, she's in big trouble.

12
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:40,059
Yeah, thanks to Kaiba, most of her
monsters are in the graveyard now.

13
00:01:40,440 --> 00:01:41,270
Oh, no.

14
00:01:41,580 --> 00:01:43,480
What if Ashisu does lose?

15
00:01:43,880 --> 00:01:46,740
Will the evil within
Merrick grow even stronger?

16
00:01:47,080 --> 00:01:49,417
She joined this tournament
to help me defeat

17
00:01:49,500 --> 00:01:52,760
her brother and to uncover
the good inside him.

18
00:01:52,900 --> 00:01:53,960
She has to win!

19
00:01:54,060 --> 00:01:56,597
Your most powerful monsters
are in the graveyard

20
00:01:56,680 --> 00:01:59,445
and soon the rest of your
cards will join them.

21
00:01:59,620 --> 00:02:01,840
I'm well aware of your plan, Kaiba.

22
00:02:03,120 --> 00:02:09,040
Seto Kaiba is so naive, believing that mere
skill can lead to victory in this game.

23
00:02:09,380 --> 00:02:12,700
That fool must accept his
ancient past in order to win.

24
00:02:13,580 --> 00:02:16,300
She has no idea what she's in for.

25
00:02:16,980 --> 00:02:19,540
Now he's coming after my magic cards.

26
00:02:20,520 --> 00:02:21,660
This is it.

27
00:02:21,920 --> 00:02:24,737
My face down card will finish you off.

28
00:02:24,820 --> 00:02:29,400
Virus Cannon, wipe out 10 magic
cards in her deck. What's this?

29
00:02:32,180 --> 00:02:36,600
I'm about to destroy your
deck, or what's left of it.

30
00:02:42,460 --> 00:02:47,460
And now, almost every magic card in your
deck has been sent to the graveyard.

31
00:02:49,500 --> 00:02:52,277
As if your deck wasn't pathetic enough.

32
00:02:52,360 --> 00:02:56,060
First, my crush card destroyed
all your high-powered monsters.

33
00:02:56,440 --> 00:02:59,357
Then my cannon did the same
thing to your magic cards.

34
00:02:59,440 --> 00:03:01,520
Your deck is no longer a threat.

35
00:03:01,800 --> 00:03:05,380
So, do you still think
I'm gonna lose? I do.

36
00:03:05,800 --> 00:03:07,817
You've played into my hands, Kaiba.

37
00:03:07,900 --> 00:03:10,000
Now, you've sealed your own fate.

38
00:03:10,880 --> 00:03:11,710
Nonsense.

39
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:14,517
I've heard enough of
your false predictions.

40
00:03:14,600 --> 00:03:16,700
My predictions are quite real.

41
00:03:16,960 --> 00:03:18,977
And now, you've fallen into my trap.

42
00:03:19,060 --> 00:03:19,900
But how?

43
00:03:20,160 --> 00:03:22,060
Your cards! They're gone!

44
00:03:22,400 --> 00:03:24,200
I still have my trap cards.

45
00:03:25,080 --> 00:03:27,160
Reveal Exchange of the Spirit!

46
00:03:27,640 --> 00:03:32,660
This trap card will be the beginning of
your downward spiral toward defeat, Kaiba.

47
00:03:33,780 --> 00:03:36,260
At a cost of 1,000 life points,

48
00:03:36,460 --> 00:03:40,857
my trap replaces the cards in each of
our decks with those in our graveyards.

49
00:03:40,940 --> 00:03:44,180
But that leaves me with
a deck of only six cards!

50
00:03:45,540 --> 00:03:46,897
So far, so good.

51
00:03:46,980 --> 00:03:49,800
I almost have the entire
paragraph translated.

52
00:03:50,260 --> 00:03:53,672
Soon we'll know exactly how
the winged dragon of Ra works.

53
00:03:53,840 --> 00:03:55,300
It won't be long now.

54
00:03:56,960 --> 00:03:59,020
Oh no, Seto's in trouble.

55
00:03:59,360 --> 00:04:01,240
Don't worry, I'm coming.

56
00:04:02,040 --> 00:04:04,360
How could I have let this happen?

57
00:04:04,780 --> 00:04:06,840
By playing Exchange of the Spirit,

58
00:04:07,200 --> 00:04:09,537
Isshisu brought all of her
powerful cards back from the

59
00:04:09,620 --> 00:04:12,940
graveyard and destroyed
Kaiba's deck at the same time.

60
00:04:13,820 --> 00:04:15,777
Isshisu hasn't lost her touch.

61
00:04:15,860 --> 00:04:20,680
She strung Kaiba along just as she
used to string me along as a child.

62
00:04:21,100 --> 00:04:25,924
Earlier, Kaiba sent almost every monster
in a Shizu's deck right to the graveyard.

63
00:04:26,180 --> 00:04:30,474
Now she gets them all back along with
the magic cards she lost last turn.

64
00:04:30,960 --> 00:04:32,780
But Kaiba's not so lucky.

65
00:04:33,080 --> 00:04:35,374
He had only six cards in his graveyard.

66
00:04:35,740 --> 00:04:39,799
Once he uses them up, his deck will
be empty and he'll lose the duel.

67
00:04:40,360 --> 00:04:42,580
I believe it's my turn, Kaiba.

68
00:04:43,140 --> 00:04:44,200
Then go.

69
00:04:44,500 --> 00:04:45,500
Very well.

70
00:04:45,860 --> 00:04:47,700
I summon Kelbeck.

71
00:04:53,280 --> 00:04:55,060
It looks like Kaiba's toast.

72
00:04:55,360 --> 00:04:58,337
There's no way he could turn
this around with just six cards.

73
00:04:58,420 --> 00:05:01,657
He still has that Egyptian God
card in his hand, doesn't he?

74
00:05:01,740 --> 00:05:03,740
Wouldn't he win if he played that?

75
00:05:03,860 --> 00:05:05,801
Look at you with all the answers.

76
00:05:06,340 --> 00:05:08,300
I'll place one card face down.

77
00:05:08,740 --> 00:05:10,000
That ends my turn.

78
00:05:10,260 --> 00:05:11,554
This is my tournament!

79
00:05:11,820 --> 00:05:13,940
If I lose, I'll be humiliated!

80
00:05:15,860 --> 00:05:18,540
I love seeing Kaiba squirm like this.

81
00:05:22,060 --> 00:05:23,820
Seto! Mokuba?

82
00:05:24,100 --> 00:05:25,580
What happened up there?

83
00:05:25,900 --> 00:05:26,980
Never mind.

84
00:05:27,320 --> 00:05:29,777
Have you finished
translating that card yet?

85
00:05:29,860 --> 00:05:30,690
Not quite yet.

86
00:05:30,920 --> 00:05:33,000
There's still one line left, Seto!

87
00:05:33,720 --> 00:05:35,180
Make your move.

88
00:05:35,300 --> 00:05:36,240
When I'm ready!

89
00:05:36,500 --> 00:05:38,200
You will pick Virus Cannon.

90
00:05:38,800 --> 00:05:39,840
Take a look.

91
00:05:40,300 --> 00:05:42,860
You have chosen Virus Cannon, correct?

92
00:05:43,680 --> 00:05:45,660
I'll take your silence as a yes.

93
00:05:45,860 --> 00:05:48,660
So go ahead and play
your trap card right now.

94
00:05:48,940 --> 00:05:51,340
You can't escape what the future holds.

95
00:05:51,660 --> 00:05:54,580
I will not listen to any
more of this nonsense.

96
00:05:54,980 --> 00:05:56,400
Activate virus cannon.

97
00:05:58,020 --> 00:06:00,860
My trap will send it
straight to the graveyard.

98
00:06:02,640 --> 00:06:03,840
Activate Muko.

99
00:06:04,160 --> 00:06:06,640
I'm afraid that's the end of your cannon.

100
00:06:06,880 --> 00:06:09,620
And soon it will be the end of you, Kaiba.

101
00:06:10,500 --> 00:06:11,440
Oh, no.

102
00:06:11,780 --> 00:06:12,640
Oh, yes.

103
00:06:13,200 --> 00:06:16,157
Have you accepted the power
of my Millennium Necklace yet?

104
00:06:16,240 --> 00:06:20,120
Or do you still deny that I have
already foreseen your defeat?

105
00:06:20,560 --> 00:06:21,860
Make your move.

106
00:06:22,120 --> 00:06:24,437
Kaiba's Dark Gremlin's
standing there doing nothing

107
00:06:24,520 --> 00:06:27,177
when everyone knows it's
stronger than her monster.

108
00:06:27,260 --> 00:06:28,966
So why isn't Kaiba attacking?

109
00:06:29,260 --> 00:06:31,620
Maybe Kaiba doesn't want to attack yet.

110
00:06:32,280 --> 00:06:33,110
Huh?

111
00:06:33,193 --> 00:06:35,457
That doesn't sound like
the Kaiba I know you.

112
00:06:35,540 --> 00:06:38,837
Yes, well, Kaiba's in quite
a tough situation here.

113
00:06:38,920 --> 00:06:41,600
He wants to summon his Egyptian god card,

114
00:06:41,760 --> 00:06:44,157
but he doesn't have enough
monsters to sacrifice.

115
00:06:44,240 --> 00:06:48,200
So, he may be planning to sacrifice
Ishizu's monsters instead.

116
00:06:48,560 --> 00:06:51,460
Oh, so that's why he's not attacking him.

117
00:06:51,840 --> 00:06:54,193
There's only one way for me to win this.

118
00:06:54,320 --> 00:06:56,680
I must summon Obelisk the Tormenter.

119
00:06:57,200 --> 00:07:02,240
Ishizu will cower in fear before the
very Egyptian god card she gave to me.

120
00:07:02,500 --> 00:07:06,140
And now I summon Zorga in attack mode.

121
00:07:13,280 --> 00:07:17,220
Soon, Kaiba will sacrifice my
monsters to summon Obelisk,

122
00:07:17,400 --> 00:07:19,340
continuing his path to defeat.

123
00:07:19,620 --> 00:07:22,440
I may only have a few
cards left in my deck,

124
00:07:22,660 --> 00:07:25,895
but I have everything I need
in order to win this duel.

125
00:07:26,120 --> 00:07:27,720
Kaiba, listen to me.

126
00:07:28,780 --> 00:07:30,340
You're in over your head.

127
00:07:30,720 --> 00:07:32,020
Stay out of this.

128
00:07:32,160 --> 00:07:35,140
This tournament of yours
is more than just a game.

129
00:07:35,560 --> 00:07:38,795
Have you not seen the damage
Merrick has caused so far?

130
00:07:38,920 --> 00:07:43,157
the people he's harmed you might
be next there is an ancient magic

131
00:07:43,240 --> 00:07:47,057
at work that cannot be denied
and if you continue to ignore it

132
00:07:47,140 --> 00:07:53,177
you're a fool all right let's go
make your move you'll regret those

133
00:07:53,260 --> 00:07:58,760
words kaiba zorgoth attack his dark
gremlin with cape of destruction

134
00:08:03,000 --> 00:08:08,920
but that's not all come forth kelbeck
and attack his life points directly

135
00:08:11,260 --> 00:08:18,097
are you done no kaiba next i'll place
this card face down and now i am

136
00:08:18,180 --> 00:08:24,317
done ishizu's face down card must be a
trap but what kind of trap is it well

137
00:08:24,400 --> 00:08:28,597
i know what i need to do avoid losing
my life points long enough to summon

138
00:08:28,680 --> 00:08:33,757
obelisk the tormentor then this duel
will be over i hope you're ready

139
00:08:33,840 --> 00:08:37,777
ready to lose that is i draw activate

140
00:08:37,860 --> 00:08:43,237
track card muco my card it goes

141
00:08:43,320 --> 00:08:47,217
straight to the graveyard looks like
kaiba's running pretty low on cards to me

142
00:08:47,300 --> 00:08:51,697
if he still wants to summon obelisk
then he better move fast you got that

143
00:08:51,780 --> 00:08:56,320
right but is it possible it's possible
but it seems like a long shot to me.

144
00:08:56,620 --> 00:08:57,800
Let's go, Seto.

145
00:08:57,960 --> 00:09:00,200
I know you can do this. Come on.

146
00:09:00,380 --> 00:09:02,937
There's no way you're going
to lose this, big brother.

147
00:09:03,020 --> 00:09:04,800
Use your secret weapon now.

148
00:09:05,940 --> 00:09:06,770
He's right.

149
00:09:06,980 --> 00:09:09,980
I have to summon Obelisk
now if I'm going to win.

150
00:09:10,220 --> 00:09:13,200
But I'll need to sacrifice
three monsters first.

151
00:09:13,520 --> 00:09:15,300
That's where Ishizu comes in.

152
00:09:15,560 --> 00:09:19,177
Once she summons a third monster,
I'll activate Soul Exchange.

153
00:09:19,260 --> 00:09:21,457
It will let me sacrifice her monsters.

154
00:09:21,540 --> 00:09:23,840
And once I do, Obelisk is mine.

155
00:09:25,280 --> 00:09:27,140
I play this face-down.

156
00:09:27,960 --> 00:09:29,480
Make your move.

157
00:09:29,840 --> 00:09:32,311
One more direct attack in Kaiba's history.

158
00:09:32,560 --> 00:09:35,736
So whatever face-down card
he played better be strong.

159
00:09:35,940 --> 00:09:39,800
If what Ashizu said is true,
there's nothing Kaiba can do to win.

160
00:09:40,080 --> 00:09:41,760
It's his destiny to lose.

161
00:09:42,840 --> 00:09:43,780
Soul Exchange.

162
00:09:44,380 --> 00:09:47,760
This is the card Kaiba will
use to sacrifice my monsters.

163
00:09:48,180 --> 00:09:51,257
He will summon the Egyptian
god I placed in his deck.

164
00:09:51,340 --> 00:09:53,380
And then victory will be mine.

165
00:09:54,020 --> 00:09:56,260
It's the beginning of the end, Kaiba.

166
00:09:57,420 --> 00:09:59,900
Now I shall place one card face down.

167
00:10:01,620 --> 00:10:02,800
Play a monster.

168
00:10:03,120 --> 00:10:06,357
She needs to have three on
the field for my plan to work.

169
00:10:06,440 --> 00:10:08,897
The face down card I've just played is the

170
00:10:08,980 --> 00:10:12,020
key to my victory and Kaiba's destruction.

171
00:10:12,460 --> 00:10:14,880
This trap card has already begun working,

172
00:10:15,180 --> 00:10:18,417
infusing one of my own monsters
with a dangerous weapon.

173
00:10:18,500 --> 00:10:22,517
A biotic blaster that will be hidden
deep within the body of my creature.

174
00:10:22,600 --> 00:10:27,600
When Kaiba sacrifices this monster,
the weapon will transfer into Obelisk.

175
00:10:28,480 --> 00:10:31,640
Now I summon the monster, Ajito!

176
00:10:35,240 --> 00:10:36,070
Excellent.

177
00:10:36,280 --> 00:10:38,620
Now the stage is set for my sacrifice.

178
00:10:39,020 --> 00:10:43,920
The way Ishizu has toyed with
Kaiba's mind is quite amusing indeed.

179
00:10:45,320 --> 00:10:46,400
Hold on!

180
00:10:46,620 --> 00:10:49,557
What if Ishizu is expecting
me to play Soul Exchange?

181
00:10:49,640 --> 00:10:52,320
I could be walking right into a trap!

182
00:10:52,600 --> 00:10:56,200
No, this is my only
chance to summon Obelisk!

183
00:10:56,360 --> 00:10:58,007
I must seize the moment now!

184
00:10:58,440 --> 00:11:00,720
Kelvek! Agido! Zorga!

185
00:11:01,080 --> 00:11:05,220
These monsters are now in my
control and will soon be sacrificed!

186
00:11:05,720 --> 00:11:07,900
Open face down card! Soul exchange!

187
00:11:09,360 --> 00:11:10,820
As I predicted.

188
00:11:13,580 --> 00:11:16,780
And now I will summon
my Egyptian God card!

189
00:11:17,860 --> 00:11:20,600
Show yourself Obelisk the Tormentor!

190
00:11:24,720 --> 00:11:34,590
Ah!

191
00:11:40,440 --> 00:11:44,900
Things are getting interesting!
Alright! Go, bro! Whoa!

192
00:11:45,180 --> 00:11:49,280
Kaiba sacrificed his Shizu's
monsters so he could summon his own!

193
00:11:49,540 --> 00:11:51,037
Still think I'm going to lose?

194
00:11:51,120 --> 00:11:55,380
Let's see which is stronger, your
necklace or my Egyptian god card.

195
00:11:56,520 --> 00:11:58,140
We shall find out.

196
00:11:58,340 --> 00:12:02,399
Counting on a piece of jewelry in
order to win this duel is pathetic.

197
00:12:02,520 --> 00:12:06,820
To win a duel takes skill and
an extremely powerful deck.

198
00:12:07,540 --> 00:12:08,900
You'll see that soon.

199
00:12:09,160 --> 00:12:14,300
When I attack you with Obelisk the
Tormenter and wipe out your life points.

200
00:12:14,680 --> 00:12:16,897
You are sadly mistaken, Kaiba.

201
00:12:16,980 --> 00:12:20,500
Ah, when I secretly played the
trap card Sacrifices Blast,

202
00:12:20,660 --> 00:12:24,120
I infused my own monster
with a self-destructing trap.

203
00:12:24,460 --> 00:12:27,620
One that now lives within
your Egyptian god monster,

204
00:12:28,000 --> 00:12:30,235
waiting to destroy it from the inside.

205
00:12:31,180 --> 00:12:37,220
When you activated Soul Exchange and
sacrificed my three monsters to summon yours,

206
00:12:37,600 --> 00:12:41,197
this secret trap card infected
Obelisk the Tormenter.

207
00:12:41,280 --> 00:12:46,800
So as soon as you use it to attack me,
your Egyptian God card will self-destruct,

208
00:12:47,040 --> 00:12:49,922
taking with it the remainder
of your life points.

209
00:12:50,500 --> 00:12:52,877
Then finally, victory will be mine.

210
00:12:52,960 --> 00:12:53,940
Try as you may.

211
00:12:54,240 --> 00:12:58,240
There's no escape from the defeat
that awaits you in your next move.

212
00:12:58,560 --> 00:12:59,460
Fat chance.

213
00:12:59,700 --> 00:13:02,180
You have no monsters left to protect you.

214
00:13:02,820 --> 00:13:05,240
So spare me the gloom and doom speech.

215
00:13:05,440 --> 00:13:07,197
And just surrender to me now.

216
00:13:07,280 --> 00:13:08,260
Yugi,

217
00:13:08,680 --> 00:13:11,317
can Ashishu be right
about Kaiba losing even

218
00:13:11,400 --> 00:13:14,224
though he has an Egyptian
god card on the field?

219
00:13:14,580 --> 00:13:16,100
Uh, Yugi?

220
00:13:16,440 --> 00:13:21,360
Ashishu predicted she'd win, but how can
Kaiba lose with Obelisk on the field?

221
00:13:21,580 --> 00:13:22,756
What's up with Yugi?

222
00:13:23,060 --> 00:13:25,197
Could her Millennium Necklace be wrong?

223
00:13:25,280 --> 00:13:28,880
Or does Ashishu have a strategy
to defend against his attack?

224
00:13:29,200 --> 00:13:30,420
Attack me, Kaiba.

225
00:13:30,960 --> 00:13:32,200
The end is here.

226
00:13:32,500 --> 00:13:35,177
No one can survive the Fury of Obelisk.

227
00:13:35,260 --> 00:13:38,820
That card belonged to me
before he even knew it existed.

228
00:13:39,180 --> 00:13:41,580
And now it shall destroy him.

229
00:13:41,940 --> 00:13:44,600
I can see the future very clearly.

230
00:13:45,200 --> 00:13:46,617
And now...

231
00:13:46,700 --> 00:13:51,100
Kaiba will be completely unaware
that my trap beats within Obelisk.

232
00:13:52,020 --> 00:13:55,140
Attack her life points directly, my beast!

233
00:13:55,560 --> 00:13:57,480
The moment it begins to attack,

234
00:13:57,800 --> 00:14:01,480
my trap card will be triggered,
destroying Obelisk and Kaiba.

235
00:14:08,000 --> 00:14:12,180
You've ridiculed my powers and
turned my own creature against me.

236
00:14:12,420 --> 00:14:13,660
Now you'll pay.

237
00:14:14,060 --> 00:14:18,040
This duel won't last much longer,
and once Kaiba's defeated,

238
00:14:18,440 --> 00:14:21,616
Ishizu will come looking for
her brother's good heart.

239
00:14:21,760 --> 00:14:23,480
She's in for a surprise.

240
00:14:24,580 --> 00:14:26,980
All right, obelisk, attack!

241
00:14:27,480 --> 00:14:29,080
Destiny is served.

242
00:14:29,340 --> 00:14:30,220
What's this?

243
00:14:30,360 --> 00:14:31,520
My Millennium Rod!

244
00:14:32,720 --> 00:14:34,960
It's activating by itself!

245
00:14:35,700 --> 00:14:37,000
What's going on?

246
00:14:38,560 --> 00:14:39,390
Obelisk!

247
00:14:40,580 --> 00:14:43,320
I feel something strange inside.

248
00:14:43,680 --> 00:14:44,960
Hey, check out Kaiba!

249
00:14:45,360 --> 00:14:47,760
For some reason, he stopped his attack!

250
00:14:48,500 --> 00:14:50,780
Yeah, but why? You okay?

251
00:14:51,220 --> 00:14:53,640
Snap out of him, bro! This is crazy!

252
00:14:54,060 --> 00:14:56,457
I've never felt anything like this before!

253
00:14:56,540 --> 00:14:58,840
Is this another one of Ishizu's tricks?

254
00:15:00,080 --> 00:15:03,660
Why are these visions
flashing before my eyes?

255
00:15:04,400 --> 00:15:06,871
Ishizu's mind games must be getting to me.

256
00:15:07,580 --> 00:15:08,720
Wait a second.

257
00:15:09,160 --> 00:15:12,336
That's the stone carving of
my blue-eyes white dragon.

258
00:15:12,520 --> 00:15:13,900
What does this mean?

259
00:15:14,500 --> 00:15:18,240
Maybe I should rethink my
strategy and call off Obelisk.

260
00:15:18,660 --> 00:15:21,720
Someone else is controlling
my Millennium Rod.

261
00:15:21,980 --> 00:15:24,200
This feeling is too strong to ignore.

262
00:15:25,220 --> 00:15:28,020
The Millennium Rod is affecting Kaiba.

263
00:15:28,480 --> 00:15:31,680
My instinct tells me
Obelisk isn't the answer.

264
00:15:33,020 --> 00:15:36,257
It's as if my Blue-Eyes
White Dragon is calling to me

265
00:15:36,340 --> 00:15:40,780
Maybe I should attack Ishizu
with Blue-Eyes instead of Obelisk

266
00:15:43,660 --> 00:15:47,877
This goes against my entire
strategy I plan to destroy

267
00:15:47,960 --> 00:15:51,320
Ishizu with Obelisk from the
beginning But now I know,

268
00:15:51,480 --> 00:15:52,700
to win this duel,

269
00:15:53,000 --> 00:15:55,680
I must summon my Blue-Eyes White Dragon

270
00:15:57,800 --> 00:16:00,580
Observe as I activate my magic card,

271
00:16:00,840 --> 00:16:05,417
Silent Doom Which lets me summon
a card from my graveyard Gadget

272
00:16:05,500 --> 00:16:10,277
soldier in defense mode This isn't
the future my necklace predicted

273
00:16:10,360 --> 00:16:14,777
Everything has changed Before
I can summon my blue eyes white

274
00:16:14,860 --> 00:16:20,780
dragon I must sacrifice two monsters
First this Oh no That's right,

275
00:16:21,140 --> 00:16:26,360
it's my Egyptian god card Ridiculous
No way man And what's he thinking?

276
00:16:26,700 --> 00:16:27,660
It can't be.

277
00:16:27,960 --> 00:16:29,060
Hear me now.

278
00:16:29,380 --> 00:16:30,900
I won't be controlled.

279
00:16:31,460 --> 00:16:33,380
I decide my future.

280
00:16:33,760 --> 00:16:36,820
So now, I sacrifice my monsters.

281
00:16:37,480 --> 00:16:41,280
Obelisk and gadget soldier, I
send you to the car graveyard.

282
00:16:41,880 --> 00:16:44,957
But how could my millennium
necklace have been wrong?

283
00:16:45,040 --> 00:16:46,660
You're so quiet, Ashisu.

284
00:16:46,960 --> 00:16:48,360
Where's your magic now?

285
00:16:48,580 --> 00:16:52,051
Or have you realized that
there's no such thing as destiny?

286
00:16:52,380 --> 00:16:55,140
Now observe as I summon my blue eyes.

287
00:16:55,300 --> 00:16:56,720
Show yourself!

288
00:17:02,200 --> 00:17:05,017
So somehow Kaiba was able to change the

289
00:17:05,100 --> 00:17:08,680
future by summoning his
blue-eyes white dragon.

290
00:17:09,580 --> 00:17:10,700
But how?

291
00:17:11,320 --> 00:17:13,140
What did he see?

292
00:17:13,520 --> 00:17:16,897
Something from Kaiba's past
must have awakened inside him,

293
00:17:16,980 --> 00:17:19,760
for he was the ancient
keeper of the blue-eyes.

294
00:17:20,360 --> 00:17:24,837
Ishizu, if you could foresee all my
moves, how did blue-eyes surprise you?

295
00:17:24,920 --> 00:17:28,640
Unless, of course, you're nothing
but a fake, as I suspected.

296
00:17:29,000 --> 00:17:30,880
Soon he shall see the truth.

297
00:17:31,360 --> 00:17:33,120
Time to finish you off now!

298
00:17:34,920 --> 00:17:37,080
Blue-Eye's white dragon, attack!

299
00:17:40,880 --> 00:17:44,620
Wipe out her life points
with white lightning attack!

300
00:17:45,960 --> 00:17:46,790
Farewell.

301
00:17:56,320 --> 00:17:58,400
Victory is mine. That's it.

302
00:17:58,640 --> 00:18:02,440
The winner of this duel
is Seto Kaiba. All right.

303
00:18:02,780 --> 00:18:06,721
I knew that you were going to win
this duel all along, big brother.

304
00:18:06,840 --> 00:18:08,040
That was insane.

305
00:18:08,680 --> 00:18:12,657
Merrick's Millennium Rod must have shown
Kaiba the secret to winning this duel.

306
00:18:12,740 --> 00:18:16,957
I bet it has something to do with the
images on that ancient stone tablet.

307
00:18:17,040 --> 00:18:19,797
Kaiba's destiny is connected
to the Blue-Eyes White Dragon,

308
00:18:19,880 --> 00:18:22,077
and I bet that's why he had to play it.

309
00:18:22,160 --> 00:18:24,219
Maybe now he'll believe in destiny.

310
00:18:24,920 --> 00:18:26,420
Very impressive, Kaiba.

311
00:18:26,880 --> 00:18:30,817
You managed to overcome the fate that
my Millennium Necklace showed me.

312
00:18:30,900 --> 00:18:33,020
Your past is the key to your power.

313
00:18:33,340 --> 00:18:36,928
I won this duel for the same
reasons I'll win the tournament.

314
00:18:37,200 --> 00:18:40,400
My superior skills and
intelligence. Perhaps.

315
00:18:40,760 --> 00:18:44,697
But you've taught me a valuable
lesson about the nature of destiny.

316
00:18:44,780 --> 00:18:46,840
And for that I am grateful, Kaiba.

317
00:18:47,620 --> 00:18:51,217
You have given me hope for
changing the future of my brother.

318
00:18:51,300 --> 00:18:56,340
Though I know the task will be
more difficult than I can imagine.

319
00:18:56,580 --> 00:19:00,677
To save the goodness trapped within,
I'll need more than my millennium powers.

320
00:19:00,760 --> 00:19:04,197
I'll need the wisdom and the
strength of the people around me,

321
00:19:04,280 --> 00:19:05,960
especially Seto Kaiba.

322
00:19:06,680 --> 00:19:09,680
The brother she knew no longer exists.

323
00:19:10,200 --> 00:19:12,080
I may have lost the duel,

324
00:19:12,420 --> 00:19:15,597
but in the process I have gained
something of far greater importance.

325
00:19:15,680 --> 00:19:20,500
The realization that if I am to win
this battle for my brother's spirit,

326
00:19:20,800 --> 00:19:22,620
I will need your help, Kaiba.

327
00:19:23,660 --> 00:19:27,820
Thank you, for I know you
will help me save my brother.

328
00:19:29,060 --> 00:19:31,460
Believe whatever you need to, Ishizu.

329
00:19:32,040 --> 00:19:34,760
But I'm only in this for myself.

330
00:19:36,300 --> 00:19:37,440
All right, Seto.

331
00:19:37,620 --> 00:19:38,855
What an awesome duel.

332
00:19:38,980 --> 00:19:41,274
You really are the best duelist I know.

333
00:19:41,400 --> 00:19:42,988
Here comes Johnny Sunshine.

334
00:19:44,840 --> 00:19:48,600
If I were you, I'd start
preparing for our duel now, Yu-Gi.

335
00:19:50,080 --> 00:19:50,910
I will.

336
00:19:50,993 --> 00:19:51,823
Good luck.

337
00:19:51,906 --> 00:19:52,860
You'll need it.

338
00:19:54,040 --> 00:19:58,100
When the time is right, Kaiba will
accept Destiny's role for him,

339
00:19:58,260 --> 00:20:01,660
and my brother and the
world will be saved.

340
00:20:14,940 --> 00:20:16,060
Yu-Gi-Oh!
